.TH FROST 1 "2026" "frost" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
frost \- small terminal text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B frost
[\fB+\fILINE\fR] [\fIFILE\fR[\fB:\fILINE\fR]]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
A small editor for the terminal: menu bar and tabs like Fresh, keys like micro (CUA clipboard, mouse, multiple cursors).
It uses the colours of your terminal. It opens files of several gigabytes at once and keeps an unlimited undo history.
.PP
Without arguments frost restores the previous session: open tabs, cursors, unsaved and untitled text, closed tabs and undo history.
With file arguments it opens only those files and leaves the saved session alone, so it is safe as $EDITOR and $VISUAL (git, nnn, crontab).
.SH KEYS
.TP
Ctrl-S, Ctrl-Q, Ctrl-O, Ctrl-N, Ctrl-W
save, quit, open, new, close tab
.TP
Ctrl-Z, Ctrl-Y, Ctrl-X, Ctrl-C, Ctrl-V
undo, redo, cut, copy, paste
.TP
Ctrl-F, F3, Ctrl-H, Ctrl-G
find, find next, replace all, go to line
.TP
Ctrl-D, Alt-Up, Alt-Down
next occurrence as a new cursor, cursor above, cursor below
.TP
Ctrl-T, Ctrl-L, Ctrl-P, F2, F1, F10
reopen closed tab, language, command palette, define word, keys, menu
.SH FILES
.TP
~/.config/frost/init.lua
configuration in Lua (theme, options, key bindings)
.TP
~/.config/frost/dictionary.txt
extra dictionary entries, one per line: word, TAB, meaning
.TP
~/.local/state/frost/
session and history
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/Gucixdev/frost
